            <div xml:id="d874">

                <pb facs="0829" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/885</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-31T14:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                                1917, 2 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 1, 1918, 3.26
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1251. My 1245 [1224], December 26 [24], 10 a.m. Finnish government sending
                    representatives to all European governments to request recognition of
                    independence. Delegation to Washington will be composed of Dr. Ignatius and
                    Professor Julio Reuter; latter now here and member of a delegation to Danish,
                    Norwegian Governments after which will proceed United States via England.
                    British Minister informs me he has been instructed to tell delegation they could
                    proceed to London and would receive sympathetic reception.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
